minimalness of the topic), the only answer is &quot;Handle it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T14:58:21-07:00","id":1511566,"title":"","content":"ritual is from thousand years of night it transfers any breaking point or humanity related banes to a victim for the nght","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T22:59:49-07:00","id":1511583,"title":"","content":"Okay, looked that up, annnnd.<br /> <br /> I mean, mostly it depends on the vampire's disposition. Memory removal, if possible, is both practical and <i>probably</i> kind, restitution of some kind after the fact is equally a good idea (particularly since there's even odds on it being cultist/herd member of the vampire's), but on the other hand, if you're the sort of person willing to use the ritual, you're probably the sort to not care about the clean up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T04:12:48-07:00","id":1511602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim#post1511550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">had a thought recently about the circle covering the cost of their institutionalization</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering the ritual (at least as described in the book) only works on a personal level (no cleaning up <b>other </b>kindred's upcoming mistakes) and the performer itself must be a master of Cruac, seems like too much work for too niche a demand - one that admiting to the existence of could be seen as a show of vulnerability to one's rivals to boot.<br /> <br /> Much safer<b><i> by far</i></b> to deal with such a issue personally (or through one's retainers &amp; herd) imho.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, if i was in the role of a blood magician aware of the existence of such ritual i would probably be <b>very</b> leery of the potential for a sympathetic link to be formed between ritualist and scapegoat through the (ab)use of such a magical feat. It seems bound to creating incidental ghouls, revenant or any such unplanned nonsense.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-14-2023, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:07:05-07:00","id":1511674,"title":"","content":"is an asylum a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T07:35:30-07:00","id":1511727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511674#post1511674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is an asylum a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>An asylum seems like too much. Forcing someone to roll breaking points on your behalf is pretty brutal, but it shouldn't permanently drive them insane. If you really care about the people you're victimizing, you should just use new people each time. The old people shouldn't be so screwed up to need institutionalization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T12:22:06-07:00","id":1511732,"title":"","content":"so give them cash anonomously","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T13:13:57-07:00","id":1511735,"title":"","content":"Or you might just not give a shit about the victim. After all, the ritual is a carte blanche for acting monstrously (for a limited time only; other consequences may still apply).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T14:53:16-07:00","id":1511738,"title":"","content":"^that. Sure, it's nice to think about how you could be fair to the victim, but if you're the kind of person who uses Scapegoat in the first place, you're probably not the person to take responsibility for the ritual's consequences in the first place-you dumped your conflicts of humanity off on someone else to avoid having to wrestle with that in the first place, so why would you suddenly have a conscience about it after the fact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T16:29:53-07:00","id":1511750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511738#post1511738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^that. Sure, it's nice to think about how you could be fair to the victim, but if you're the kind of person who uses Scapegoat in the first place, you're probably not the person to take responsibility for the ritual's consequences in the first place-you dumped your conflicts of humanity off on someone else to avoid having to wrestle with that in the first place, so why would you suddenly have a conscience about it after the fact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one might keep the person under wraps at least for the night, due to any potential risks related to sympathetic magic links, but that's just my personal occult paranoia talking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T17:19:25-07:00","id":1511752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511732#post1511732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so give them cash anonomously</div> </div> </div> </div>The ritual has you feed the victim your blood, anonymity probably isn't an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T17:26:18-07:00","id":1511753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511752#post1511752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ritual has you feed the victim your blood, anonymity probably isn't an option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just a mug of strong, bitter coffe with rum. Never underestimate what Dominate &amp;/or Obfuscate can do for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T19:13:11-07:00","id":1511761,"title":"","content":"<br /> In the original ritual from whence this ritual takes its name wasn't the scape goat slain at the end of was it the one allowed to run off free?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> A slow acting poison, administered at the same time as the blood, could do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T19:41:33-07:00","id":1511763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511761#post1511761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original ritual from whence this ritual takes its name wasn't the scape goat slain at the end of was it the one allowed to run off free?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the one that fled, correct.<br /> <br /> One thing I haven't really seen answered, and is probably confusing the answers, is &quot;to what end are we talking about dealing with the victim?&quot; The Original Poster seems to be leaning in the direction of doing right by/making it up to the victim, but as has been mentioned, we've seen answers concerned with keeping secrecy, addressing mystical side effects, and other such things, and while coming up with an answer that best addresses as many reason to do something about a victim as possible, specificity will probably be more serviceable.<br /> <br /> And because I haven't hit the morality drum enough in this topic(because the OP seems interested in moral correction), we should also take a moment to mention that in the grab bag of morally questionable tools available to the Kindred, Scapegoat is kind of one of the worst because there's essentially no good or even justifiable reason to use it. The closest you get is that something needs to be done (and for the purposes of this, let's say whatever example we manage to conjure up fits a mostly mutual agreement of &quot;needs must at times like this&quot;) and the risk of it not getting done are present due to the low humanity of the vampire who has to do this, and even in that instance it's still a better argument that the vampire needs bear the burden of risking their humanity while doing this thing what definitely, inargubly must be done than to inflict on someone else. Pretty much any argument is just creating an excuse, and by extension any thing done to help the victim, while still a good and decent thing to do, is basically an extension of those excuses.<br /> <br /> THis isn't like where a vampire carefully selects people to feed from people who can afford to take a day off the next day and otherwise covers for any loss of resources or security brought on by the time of wooziness from blood loss-Scapegoat's pretty firmly in the &quot;afflict another so you can be comfortable&quot; category of power exercise, and no amount of paying for therapy will quite cover for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T20:36:05-07:00","id":1511765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511763#post1511763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The closest you get is that something needs to be done (and for the purposes of this, let's say whatever example we manage to conjure up fits a mostly mutual agreement of &quot;needs must at times like this&quot;) and the risk of it not getting done are present due to the low humanity of the vampire who has to do this, and even in that instance it's still a better argument that the vampire needs bear the burden of risking their humanity while doing this thing what definitely, inargubly must be done than to inflict on someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's enough systems of morality you can pretty much always find one or another to justify actions. Let's agree there's something that needs doing and your two options are do it after doing this ritual or just do it. Let's further assume this is going to have pretty severe consequences for whomever takes the morality hit, 3-4 points at least. <br /> <br /> I could argue that it would be more moral to let a random and average person take that morality hit rather than have a super powerful immortal being taking the hit. The possibilities for collateral damage from the loss of humanity are much lower with the mortal, from both a power perspective and from a timeline perspective. <br /> <br /> Then we can get into what if the scape goat is willingly participating in the ritual? What if the victim is going to die of natural causes imminently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T20:58:54-07:00","id":1511769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1511550-scapegoat-ritual-what-to-do-with-victim?p=1511765#post1511765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's enough systems of morality you can pretty much always find one or another to justify actions. Let's agree there's something that needs doing and your two options are do it after doing this ritual or just do it. Let's further assume this is going to have pretty severe consequences for whomever takes the morality hit, 3-4 points at least.<br /> <br /> I could argue that it would be more moral to let a random and average person take that morality hit rather than have a super powerful immortal being taking the hit. The possibilities for collateral damage from the loss of humanity are much lower with the mortal, from both a power perspective and from a timeline perspective.<br /> <br /> Then we can get into what if the scape goat is willingly participating in the ritual? What if the victim is going to die of natural causes imminently?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you can <i>argue</i> it. But as I mentioned, at the end of the day, it's all excuses. In the abstract, there's any number of things that a vampire can do to better roll with the humanity punches and otherwise be better for handling the hypothetical, and specificity will only reveal all the more reasons why someone can do anything but Scapegoat, in that namely there's realistically no situation so fraught that justifies the use of Scapegoat but doesn't have the time to come up with just about any other kind of answer, almost invariably also ensuring that an actor who's that at risk isn't on the field, with just about any exception that can be made up having been made so to justify the decision and not the other way around. Even getting consent for doing it to a person is a dubious affair, because there's really just no way of preparing to have the full knowledge of what they're getting into, and thus can't ever fully make an informed choice on the first go. Later uses can be argued as more moral from that point, but there's no dodging that initial barrier, and again the purpose of the ritual speaks against the sort of people invested in doing this.<br /> <br /> This is one of those &quot;I don't care how many kittens you pull from trees, this is not a thing a good person does&quot; things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}